cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Design, verification and pre-registration for: What does thermodynamic structure buy a
  learned model of a temperature-swing adsorption column?
message: If you use this software or its design, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Abdulhamid
    family-names: Batayhi
    email: abdulhamid.batayhi@std.yildiz.edu.tr
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0374-6755"
    affiliation: >-
      Yıldız Technical University, Faculty of Mechanical Engineering, Department of Mechatronics Engineering, Istanbul, Türkiye
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdulhamidbatayhi123/ai-column-structure"
abstract: >-
  The pre-registered design of a computational study that asks what thermodynamic structure
  buys a learned reduced model of a non-isothermal adsorption column (a MOF water-harvesting
  bed). Energy and entropy are fixed from the adsorbent's and the gas's thermodynamics, not
  learned; inlet, outlet and wall are ports. The repository holds the thermodynamic
  formulation, its numerical verification on small grids (it reduces to the Paper 1 solver to
  better than 1e-8), property tests, a number gate that binds every quoted number to its
  results file, the literature journals behind the gap statement, two independent review
  rounds, the correction ledger and the draft pre-registration. No study data exist yet; the
  pre-registration is frozen only after the author's review and a pilot.
keywords:
  - metriplectic
  - GENERIC
  - port-Hamiltonian
  - structure-preserving machine learning
  - reduced-order model
  - adsorption column
  - temperature-swing adsorption
  - metal-organic frameworks
  - water harvesting
  - pre-registration
license: MIT
